    "published_at": null,
    "image_url": null,
    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71671287\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><span class=\"drop-caps\">I</span>n 2025, the luxury house Balenciaga released an expensive tote that looked, to most eyes, like an ordinary plastic grocery bag. Eight years earlier, in Navi Mumbai, a shopkeeper lost his life after refusing a customer an extra carry bag. One story belongs to the fashion pages, the other to the crime columns. However, both place a single object at the centre of contention, and I think that object deserves more attention than we usually give it.</p><p>In India, we call it plastic irrespective of what it is made of: polythene, paper, cloth or laminated card. Our conversation about it is almost entirely ecological, and rightly so. The clogged drains, the ban notices and the cattle feeding on roadside refuse are real. Let us set that debate aside for a moment, not because it matters less, but because it has obscured something else. The bag is also a social document. It records where we shop, and it announces that record to everyone we rub our shoulders with.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 08, 2026 04:50 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71671287\" data-title=\"The bag that speaks\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/the-bag-that-speaks/article71671287.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-a9cb38247649b6d4595face4-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/the-bag-that-speaks/article71671287.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=The%20bag%20that%20speaks&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fthe-bag-that-speaks%2Farticle71671287.ece\" target=\"_self\">\n                    Email     \n                                \n                </a></li><li class=\"facebook\" data-cf-modified-a9cb38247649b6d4595face4-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; openShareLink('https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fthe-bag-that-speaks%2Farticle71671287.ece&amp;t=The%20bag%20that%20speaks')\">\n                Facebook   \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"twitter\" data-cf-modified-a9cb38247649b6d4595face4-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; openShareLink('https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fthe-bag-that-speaks%2Farticle71671287.ece&amp;text=The%20bag%20that%20speaks')\">\n                Twitter    \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"telegram\" data-cf-modified-a9cb38247649b6d4595face4-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; openShareLink('https://t.me/share/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fthe-bag-that-speaks%2Farticle71671287.ece&amp;text=The%20bag%20that%20speaks')\">\n                Telegram     \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"in\" data-cf-modified-a9cb38247649b6d4595face4-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; openShareLink('https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fthe-bag-that-speaks%2Farticle71671287.ece&amp;title=The%20bag%20that%20speaks')\">\n                LinkedIn     \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"what